{"_v":1,"id":"peter-and-the-starcatcher-2012","cat":"broadway","cs":73.01,"rc":8,"bd":{"positive":6,"mixed":0,"negative":2},"rv":[{"cn":"David Cote","o":"Time Out New York","s":79,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"http://www.timeout.com/newyork/comedy/peter-and-the-starcatcher-1","q":"And you can be sure: Peter soars—deliriously high and gloriously far."},{"cn":"Mark Kennedy","o":"Associated Press","s":44,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.huffpost.com/huff-wires/20120415/us-theater-review-peter-and-the-starcatcher/","d":"2012-04-15","q":"It's supposed to connect with kids and adults alike, but ends up shortchanging both with a frantic, indulgent mess."},{"cn":"David Sheward","o":"Backstage","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.backstage.com/bso/content_display/reviews/ny-theatre-reviews/e3i5962732c3922cddeb067c9f3848f8274","q":"I'm happy to report that \"Peter\" has not given up a speck of its fairy dust–infused whimsy."},{"cn":"Howard Shapiro","o":"The Philadelphia Inquirer","s":78,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://articles.philly.com/2012-04-15/news/31345427_1_starcatcher-alex-timbers-christian-borle","d":"2012-04-15","q":"Adults will enjoy its complex theatricality... Kids will follow it for its bizarre and hammy characters and its constant sense of adventure."},{"cn":"Michael Musto","o":"Village Voice","s":76,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://blogs.villagevoice.com/dailymusto/2012/04/peter_and_the_s.php","q":"Peter catches enough stardust, especially when it's at its most wicked."},{"cn":"Melissa Rose Bernardo","o":"Entertainment Weekly","s":54,"b":"Negative","t":2,"u":"https://www.ew.com/ew/article/0,,20364394_20587320,00.html","q":"Peter and the Starcatcher still suffers from the same identity crisis that it exhibited during its 2011 run."},{"cn":"Lucy Komisar","o":"The Komisar Scoop","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://www.thekomisarscoop.com/2012/12/peter-and-the-starcatcher-is-enormously-clever-wildly-comic-peter-pan-prequel/","d":"2012-12-23","q":"This is a theater classic every bit as much as “Peter Pan” was."},{"cn":"Sarah Taylor Ellis","o":"Stage and Cinema","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://stageandcinema.com/2012/09/09/peter-starcatcher/","d":"2012-04-18","q":"Under the swift and farcical direction of Roger Rees and Alex Timbers, the company glows like starstuff itself."}],"au":{"score":83.6,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"mz":{"s":83,"c":137,"sr":4.1},"ss":{"s":86,"c":12}}},"tn":[{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Featured Actor in a Play","n":"Christian Borle","w":true},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Scenic Design of a Play","n":"Donyale Werle","w":true},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Costume Design of a Play","n":"Paloma Young","w":true},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Lighting Design of a Play","n":"Jeff Croiter","w":true},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Sound Design of a Play","n":"Darron L. West","w":true},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Play","n":null},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Original Score","n":"Wayne Barker"},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Original Score","n":"Rick Elice"},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Featured Actress in a Play","n":"Celia Keenan-Bolger"},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Direction of a Play","n":"Roger Rees"},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Direction of a Play","n":"Alex Timbers"},{"yr":66,"cat":"Best Original Score","n":null}],"cn":{"t":"Critics praise the imaginative stagecraft and talented cast, though some worry the show's intimate charm was diminished in the move from Off-Broadway to the larger Brooks Atkinson Theatre.","rc":9},"bo":{"tw":null,"at":{"g":17698854,"p":337,"a":255200}},"hi":"/images/shows/peter-and-the-starcatcher-2012/hero.webp","ta":"256 W 47th St, New York, NY 10036","vs":{"sl":4,"so":4,"co":2,"am":4,"fa":3},"pd":"2012-03-28","ca":[{"n":"Christian Borle","r":"Black Stache"},{"n":"Adam Chanler-Berat","r":"Boy"},{"n":"Celia Keenan-Bolger","r":"Molly"},{"n":"Teddy Bergman","r":"Fighting Prawn"},{"n":"Arnie Burton","r":"Mrs. Bumbrake"},{"n":"Matt D'Amico","r":"Slank"},{"n":"Kevin Del Aguila","r":"Smee"},{"n":"Carson Elrod","r":"Prentiss"},{"n":"Greg Hildreth","r":"Alf"},